WHATNOW

What tam-knox is doing now and what comes next. Read this first;
revise it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-25, with W1

STATE

  Version 0.1.2 on branch dev. Initial multi-repository Git workbench
  and file viewer is complete, with high-contrast 256-color selection
  and header styling for tam-last, dynamic repo-name column sizing, and
  g / Ctrl+G keybinding guidance toggle, and passes make test, make
  sanitize, and idol-check (W1).

  Features working in 0.1.0:
  - Multi-repository Source Control sidebar (repository discovery,
    branch name, dirty/clean state, changed files list, ahead/behind
    count, path-scoped staging and committing, and remote sync with
    protected-branch confirmation for main and test).
  - Git Graph commit history using the Vertex/Branch/determinePath lane
    layout algorithm from mhutchie.git-graph, with inline ref badges and
    a split Commit Details and Changed Files diff inspector.
  - Folder Explorer tree with live Git status badges.
  - File and Diff Viewer with C11 syntax coloring and tam-view Markdown,
    HTML, and Mermaid rendering, tabs, split panes, command palette, and
    keybinding guidance.

NEXT

  1. P2 (0.2.0): Interactive branch checkout / creation modal, stash
     list management, and side-by-side diff split view.
  2. P3 (0.3.0): File tree substring filter, multi-repo batch fetch, and
     optional user keymap.ini configuration via libtam tam_ini.

WAITING FOR FRED

  Nothing.

WATCH OUT

  - Never invoke git commit -a or git add -A: tam-knox commits only the
    explicitly staged file paths in the active repository.
  - Pushing main or test always requires explicit user confirmation.
  - Follow tamlinux/arch/keybindings.md: no Meta bindings, no Alt+Left/
    Right or Alt+F1..F12, and no double-acting Ctrl codes.
